From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:34:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] util, vulkan: the PS4's FreeBSD 9 kernel and its libc

- futex: the PS4 runs FreeBSD 9's kernel, whose UMTX_OP_WAIT_UINT takes a
  relative struct timespec (struct _umtx_time came with FreeBSD 10).
  futex_wait() converts the absolute CLOCK_MONOTONIC timeout for it and,
  as on Linux, fails with -1 and errno.
- os_file: there is no kinfo_file for os_same_file_description.
- memstream: the PS4's libc has no open_memstream. Detect it
  (HAVE_OPEN_MEMSTREAM) and, where it is missing, back u_memstream with
  tmpfile() as on Windows. The RADV hang report goes through u_memstream,
  and ac_get_umr_waves, which needs umr anyway, is left out.
- vk_device: FreeBSD's CLOCK_MONOTONIC_FAST is not CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW but
  CLOCK_MONOTONIC at tick granularity, which reads behind a precise
  reading taken before it; without CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW the raw time
  domain is not offered.

Co-authored-by: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3DbSodVLhQVcvZSazbPue
